BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Nadja Lubiw-Hazard: Tizzy and Me: Fifteen Ways to Love a Mink
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260620T113000
UID:6a060ada748daf857d58a442@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join author and veterinarian Nadja Lubiw-Hazard for an interac
 tive storytelling program as she reads from her children's chapter book\, 
 Tizzy and Me: Fifteen Ways to Love a Mink. The story is narrated by spunky
  seven-year-old Georgia\, who lives with her two moms and their dog\, Tizz
 y. This story celebrates animal activism and 2SLGBTQ+ families. Following 
 the reading\, there will be a Q&A with the author\, and a storytelling act
 ivity using story stones.\nNadja is a veterinarian turned writer. She writ
 es for both adults and children. As a life-long animal lover and long time
  advocate for them\, Nadja loves to share her passion for animals and natu
 re wherever she goes. She lives in Toronto with her wife\, and a fluffy fe
 isty white cat.\nNo registration required. For children aged 6-12.
LOCATION:Hillcrest\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a060ada748daf857d58a442
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
