DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260709T150000
UID:6a11b20cf56bd86e00b18cc5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to make environmentally-friendly\, recycled\, handma
 de paper in this fun\, easy\, and interactive workshop. Leave with sheets 
 of beautiful\, one-of-a-kind paper plus the knowledge that you did somethi
 ng great for the earth!\nParticipants will learn about the ancient craft o
 f papermaking\, and have an opportunity to make their own beautiful\, recy
 cled paper from paper scraps\, plus a variety of techniques to further cus
 tomize their sheets.\nFor children ages 9-12.\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the\nPublic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and
  20(d). The information will only be used for\nevent and program registrat
 ion\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library\nhandles yo
 ur information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 
 416-397-\n5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
